# Local build output. NOT committed from dev machines — CI is the sole producer
# of web/dist (its build step force-adds it via `git add -f web/dist`). This stops
# macOS-built and Linux-built wasm from churning 85MB diffs against each other.
#
# Ignoring dist/ alone wasn't enough: once CI force-added it, dist became a
# tracked path, and .gitignore never applies to tracked files — so every local
# build showed up as a modified 67MB wasm and got swept into commits, which then
# conflicted with CI's own rebuild on the next pull. Local builds now go to
# dist-local instead (see build.sh); only CI writes dist.
.build/
dist/
dist-local/
